# This is a Windows-first repository: every text file is CRLF in the working tree, always.
#
# Enforced here rather than left to whatever tool last wrote a file. Editors, scripts and anything
# running under WSL will happily write bare LF -- Python's open() in text mode does it by default -- and
# a batch file is the one place it can actually bite, because cmd.exe has historically been unreliable
# about `goto` and multi-line blocks in an LF-only script. Pinning it in git means a fresh clone is
# correct no matter what produced the file.
#
# git stores LF internally and converts on checkout, so this costs nothing in the history and keeps
# diffs clean.
* text=auto eol=crlf
*.yml text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Binaries git must not touch or try to convert.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.icns   binary
*.dll    binary
*.exe    binary
*.pdb    binary
*.so     binary
*.dylib  binary
*.zip    binary
*.gz     binary
*.tar    binary
*.7z     binary
